  "body": "## What changed\n\n`web/build-app-wasm.sh`: the `--config patch.crates-io...` build makes cargo rewrite the workspace `Cargo.lock` (flecs_ecs 0.2.2 / flecs_ecs_sys 0.2.1 lose `source` and `checksum`). The script now saves the tracked lock to `target/wasm-tools/Cargo.lock.keep` before its first cargo call (moved up from step 3, so `cargo fetch` and the wasm-bindgen install are covered too), and an `EXIT` trap restores it on success, failure and Ctrl-C/TERM. The header documents this; the only gap is SIGKILL, where the header says to run `git checkout -- Cargo.lock`.\n\nNote: the main-branch script already had a restore trap on the cargo build step. The bug as filed reproduces only without it (a direct cargo call with the same `--config` dirties `Cargo.lock`). This PR moves the save/trap ahead of every cargo call and documents it.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/949-wasm-script-lock.md` (restore-from-copy chosen over a temp manifest dir).\n\n## Readings (run in the worktree, `git status --short`)\n\n- Before the change, direct cargo with the same `--config` patches: ` M Cargo.lock` (bug reproduced).\n- Failed run, new script (wasm32 target not installed, so cargo fails after resolving): exit 101, `error[E0463]: can't find crate for core`; `git status --short` shows only the script edit, `Cargo.lock` clean.\n- Interrupt check with the same save/restore shape and a 30 s step: lock dirty mid-run (` M Cargo.lock`), clean after SIGINT (EXIT trap runs on signal exit).\n- `bash -n web/build-app-wasm.sh`: ok.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A successful full wasm build: the wasm32-unknown-unknown target is not installed on the test machine, so the success path was not run. It uses the same EXIT trap, but this is unverified by a real success run.\n- No test was added. The repo has no shell-test harness, and a grep-style \"script contains the trap\" test would prove little. The readings above are the proof.\n- No PowerShell twin exists (`web/` has only `build-app-wasm.sh`), so nothing to fix there.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `web/` scripts may be marked `needs-maintainer` by the PR reviewer as scripts; that is expected.\n- Not a process file (not in AGENTS.md's list), so no `PROCESS_VERSION` bump.\n- Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nChangelog: none (build tooling)\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #949\n",
